{"id": "unknown-2026-07-11-001", "date": "2026-07-11", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 28, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Textile focus of China’s 2026-2030 Five-Year Plan signals capacity war", "content": "China’s 15th Five-Year Plan aims to expand textile capacity despite a ~30 per cent fall in US import prices since 2019. \nUS Section 301 cases propose 10-12.5 per cent textile duties plus a US-input incentive before end-2026. \nChina+1 remains exposed: Bangladesh sourced 58.3 per cent of textiles and 87.4 per cent of knitted fabrics from China in Q1 2026. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/textile-focus-of-china-s-2026-2030-five-year-plan-signals-capacity-war-311668-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
